// XR2.11.1 (Oscar, 12 Nov, in the copy chat: what repeats, or was already ruled out, comes off with nothing in its place): the hero has no paragraph (headline and button only) and the "Ring-fenced" line is gone. // XR2.11 (Oscar, 12 Nov: "We are using version 31E and merging the other changes"): the Captives page is board XR2.9.31E. Beside the headline a disk of stars turns about an empty centre; scrolling whirls it, flattens it into one ring a cell and grows it to the size it keeps beside the list, where the Tabit knot gathers in stars at its centre; a mouse over a cell turns its ring Brass and names it. The figure is drawn by this module's js (readable source: tools/captives_figure.js), which TabitPage.tsx runs. The list runs shortest name first, because its order is the rings' order, inner to outer. Copy as agreed on 11 and 12 Nov (nine cells, "Why Tabit" and the closing headline gone, American spelling). The Home link is the word alone. XR2.10 (Oscar, 12 Nov): no sky of its own; the page is clear and the home's own live sky shows behind it (TabitSite.js mountTabitSky, mounted by TabitPage.tsx / TabitArticle.tsx). Earlier: Ashleigh11.11 (XR2.8): menu "Press" now goes to /press; the sky is the home-matched star tile (images/tabit-sky-tile.jpg). Earlier: Tabit XR2.9.7: text never smaller than 1 unit = 1 px above phone width; two columns need 1024 px and 1.6:1. XR2.9.6: sizes follow the width only, never the window height. Earlier: XR2.9.2 captives page: the approved copy restyled to STYLE.md v1.1 (built by x9/build292.py from the design canvas, Beta 4.2 Live).
